---
import PageLayout from '../layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../lib/site';
import { withBase } from '../lib/paths';

const updated = '2026-07-28';
---

<PageLayout
  title="Terms of Use"
  description={`Rules for using the ${siteConfig.name} website and content.`}
>
  <p class="note">Last updated: {updated}</p>

  <p>
    By using {siteConfig.name} at {siteConfig.origin}{siteConfig.basePath}, you agree to these terms.
    If you do not agree, do not use the Site.
  </p>

  <h2>Editorial content</h2>
  <p>
    Articles are for general information. We aim for accuracy and cite sources, but we do not
    guarantee completeness or fitness for a particular purpose. Nothing on the Site is investment,
    legal, or professional advice.
  </p>

  <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
  <p>
    Site design, original writing, and branding are owned by us or our licensors. You may link to
    articles and quote short excerpts with attribution and a link back. Do not scrape the Site for
    wholesale republication without permission.
  </p>
  <p>
    Images credited to third parties remain those parties’ property; we use them under fair use /
    news reporting context or rights as described in each article’s sources.
  </p>

  <h2>User submissions</h2>
  <p>
    If you send tips or form messages, you grant us a non-exclusive right to use that information
    to operate the publication (including following up and, where appropriate, reporting with your
    consent or as otherwise lawful).
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party links</h2>
  <p>
    Articles link to company sites, press, and other outlets. We are not responsible for third-party
    content or privacy practices.
  </p>

  <h2>Disclaimer</h2>
  <p>
    The Site is provided “as is.” To the fullest extent permitted by law, we disclaim warranties and
    are not liable for damages arising from use of the Site or reliance on its content.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>We may update these terms; continued use after changes means you accept the revised terms.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.emails.contact}`}>{siteConfig.emails.contact}</a> ·
    <a href={withBase('contact')}>Contact form</a> ·
    <a href={withBase('privacy')}>Privacy Policy</a>
  </p>
</PageLayout>
